# 027 · One Logs page

**Status:** `DROPPED`, merged into [252](252-usage-logs-settings.goal) · **Version:** [v0.3.0](../roadmap.md#v030)

## What

One Logs page in the dashboard. The audit log becomes one category beside control's requests, refusals, failures, rig lifecycle and background jobs (model lists, renewals, machine and cluster checks). Filters by category, rig and time.

## Why

When something fails in a running control, the operator must find out why from the dashboard.

## Done when

- [ ] Every line control logs is on the page, and it can be filtered.
- [ ] A mockup was approved before the build.

## Decisions

- 2026-10-19, owner: The audit log becomes "Logs", with audit as one category, and every log from control is visible there.
- 2026-11-10, the owner, with the v0.3.0 plan (goal [242](_completed/242-v030-review.goal)): merged into [252](252-usage-logs-settings.goal). Logs is a place of the new dashboard (goal 252).

## Open questions

None.

## Progress

- 2026-10-19: Goal written from the roadmap.
- 2026-11-10: Merged into goal 252.

